      "body": "Swept the lexer's other word reservations against the editor text path (roundtrip through Parser.to_zipper/MakeTerm). Same class as Nat/Bool, on the expression side: `let poly = 1 in 2`, `let named_fun = 1 in 2`, `let rec = 1 in 2`, `let end = 1 in 2`, `let then = 1 in 2` all roundtrip cleanly as variables in the editor but fail menhir outright \u2014 the lexer emits POLY/NAMED_FUN/REC/END/THEN unconditionally.\n\nThe filter words (`eval`, `pause`, `debug`, `hide`) plus `use`/`fix`/`test`/`hint`/`typfun` are keywords on both sides, so no parity gap there \u2014 but menhir hard-errors where the editor degrades to incomplete tiles; a demo program using `let eval = \u2026` tripped the FastParseCorpus ratchet that way. Whatever contextual-keyword treatment fixes the type names should cover the five identifier-legal words above too.",
